# 0193 — Timeline chronological events

## Mission

Chronological event presentation for sessions, tasks, deployments, traces, and
agent turns: timestamps, relative time, duration, actor, status, grouping,
expansion, correlation, filters, live streaming with preserved reading position,
recipes (rail / detailed / grouped-day), no-color symbols+labels, and composition
with CheckpointTimeline, LogStream, and task history.

Research: Git history, CI timelines, observability tools, agent session views.

## Preserve / migrate / split / delete

| Surface | Fate |
|---------|------|
| `Timeline` / `TimelineEvent` names | **Preserved** (moved to `timeline` module) |
| `TimelineEvent { when, text, active }` | **Migrated** → builders; fields remain, many optional added |
| Stateless `Widget` paint | **Preserved** for unit-id events (`TimelineEvent::new`) |
| `progress_steps_as_timeline_events` | **Migrated** to builders |
| `TimelineState` / `TimelineOutcome` / recipes / status | **Added** |
| `CheckpointTimeline` | **Added** (restore/compare outcomes on Timeline substrate) |
| `filter_timeline_events` | **Added** |
| Nothing deleted | Agent ToolCard/ThinkingBlock unchanged |

## Consumer edits

```diff
- TimelineEvent { when: "12:01", text: "Started", active: false }
+ TimelineEvent::new("12:01", "Started")
+ // or with id:
+ TimelineEvent::with_id("e1", "12:01", "Started deploy")
+     .status(TimelineStatus::Success)
+     .actor("ci")
+     .relative("1h ago")

- frame.render_widget(Timeline::new(&events, system), area);
+ let mut state = TimelineState::new();
+ // Live stream: state.following = true; state.on_append(events.len());
+ frame.render_stateful_widget(
+     Timeline::with_events(&events, system)
+         .recipe(TimelineRecipe::Detailed) // or Rail / GroupedDay
+         .focused(true),
+     area,
+     &mut state,
+ );

  // Checkpoints:
+ CheckpointTimeline::new(&ckpts, system).render(area, buf, &mut state);
+ // Enter → RestoreRequested; c → CompareRequested
```

### Live stream law

- Default `following = true` pins cursor to newest.
- Scroll-up / move-up sets `following = false` (preserve reading position).
- `f` or End re-follows; `on_append` only advances when following.

### Stories

- `timeline/basic`, `rail`, `grouped`, `streaming`, `checkpoint` (+ narrow/unicode)

